# CNX Ad Server configuration: the ONLY place this app's publisher-specific values live.
#
# Copy this file to app/cnx.properties (it is gitignored, so your values are never committed) and
# fill in every value. The build fails, naming each missing or malformed value, until you do.
#
# --- Before you start ---
#
# Ads only play when your account is set up for them. None of the following can be checked from the
# app. Most of them fail the same way: the auction returns no ad, and the event log shows
# "AD_ERROR 10064 No ad available".
#
#  1. Your JW Player account is enabled for Ad Server. Ask your JW Player account manager if unsure.
#  2. You have an App Player in the JW dashboard property you will use: Players > In-app tab. It exists
#     only to give you a player ID for targeting and analytics; styling and player settings come from
#     the SDK, not from the dashboard.
#  3. Your Ad Server line items, creatives and targeting rules are in that same property.
#  4. Your app includes the jwplayer-cnx and jwplayer-ima modules (see app/build.gradle). Some auctions
#     are won by ads that only Google IMA can render, and without it those breaks fail.
#  5. Your app is registered for ad serving. Registration is not self-service: contact JW Player
#     support to register a new app or confirm an existing registration, and ask which application ID
#     it is registered under. That is the value REGISTERED_APPLICATION_ID must hold.
#
# --- Required values ---

# Your JW Player license key.
# Where to find it: JW dashboard > [your property] > API Credentials > JW Player License Keys.
# It must come from the SAME property as APP_PLAYER_ID.
LICENSE_KEY=

# The ID of your App Player: exactly 8 letters and digits, e.g. a1B2c3D4.
# Where to find it: JW dashboard > [your property] > Players > In-app tab > [your App Player].
# It scopes ad requests to this placement; the license key identifies the account.
APP_PLAYER_ID=

# The application ID (package name) your app is registered under for ad serving, e.g. com.example.myapp.
# This is the app identity the ad service checks, so it decides whether ads play at all.
# In your own app this is normally your applicationId. It is a separate value here because this sample
# is built as com.jwplayer.demo.cnxadserverbpa, which is not registered for ad serving; the app passes
# it to CnxAdvertisingConfig.Builder.bundleID(...), which overrides the package name the SDK would
# otherwise send.
REGISTERED_APPLICATION_ID=
